      id: "hook-28", type: "hook",
      content: "In 2016 the Chairperson of the NHRC — a former Chief Justice of India, Justice H.L. Dattu — publicly called his own institution a 'toothless tiger'. The Supreme Court used the same phrase about it in the Manipur extra-judicial killings case. And in 2017 the global body that accredits national human rights institutions downgraded India's NHRC from 'A' grade. How does a commission headed by retired Chief Justices, with the powers of a civil court, end up describing itself as toothless?",
